.SS help
this screen, or a command's or subcommand's help (as COMMAND \-\-help)
.PP
.nf
\fBprobbit\fR help [COMMAND [SUBCOMMAND]]
.fi
.PP
Print the help of a command or subcommand, the same text as `probbit COMMAND [SUBCOMMAND] \-\-help`; alone, the same as `probbit \-\-help`.
.PP
Examples:
.RS 4
.nf
probbit help persona fuzz
.fi
.RE
.SS completions
a completion script for bash, zsh or fish: commands, subcommands, flags
.PP
.nf
\fBprobbit\fR completions bash|zsh|fish
.fi
.PP
Print a static completion script for the shell: the commands, subcommands and flags (with their help where the shell shows it), generated from the same table as this help, so it lists exactly what the parser accepts. Regenerate it after an upgrade.
.PP
\fIinstall\fR: bash: probbit completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/probbit zsh: probbit completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_probbit, with fpath=(~/.zfunc $fpath) before compinit in ~/.zshrc fish: probbit completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/probbit.fish
.PP
\fIexit\fR: 0 the script, 2 no shell or an unknown one (the list of shells on stderr).
.PP
Examples:
.RS 4
.nf
probbit completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_probbit
source <(probbit completions bash)
.fi
.RE
.SS man
the manual page (roff), generated from this table: probbit man | man \-l \-
.PP
.nf
\fBprobbit\fR man
.fi
.PP
Print the manual page in roff (man(7) macros): NAME, SYNOPSIS, DESCRIPTION, COMMANDS (every command, subcommand and flag of this help), EXIT STATUS, ENVIRONMENT, EXAMPLES, SEE ALSO. The release archives carry it as docs/probbit.1 and install.sh installs it to ~/.local/share/man/man1/, or to <prefix>/share/man/man1/ when PROBBIT_INSTALL_DIR is <prefix>/bin.
.PP
Examples:
.RS 4
.nf
probbit man | man \-l \-
probbit man > ~/.local/share/man/man1/probbit.1
.fi
.RE
.SS version
print the version (also \-\-version, \-V)
.PP
.nf
\fBprobbit\fR version
.fi
.PP
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 done or an answer; 1 an answer that says no (infeasible, a line that differs, a counterexample, a rule left unknown); 2 a bad command, flag or input (a line on stderr; for bad input also one {"error"} object on stdout when stdout is not a terminal); 3 refused / declined / non\-finite (decide, run, evaluate), or a rule left unproven (persona lint); 4 refused by a lock, a pause or a retirement (live); 5 a strand with a field or line kind this engine does not know (live verify: unsupported, not verified and not a divergence). Each command's \-\-help has its own list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
PROBBIT_CHAINS, PROBBIT_THREADS, PROBBIT_CPU_LIMIT, PROBBIT_MEM_LIMIT_MB, PROBBIT_PRIORITY: the processor controls (flag > environment > probbit.json, or the file PROBBIT_CONFIG names > default). NO_COLOR=1 or PROBBIT_THEME=plain: no colour on a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
probbit demo | probbit decide \-\-summary \-\-pretty
probbit run \-\-pretty < examples/knapsack\-20.json
probbit persona init examples/persona/tutor.yaml \-\-out pip.json
probbit live examples/persona/tutor.yaml \-\-seed 2 \-\-demo week
probbit monitor \-\-demo \-\-open
claude mcp add probbit \-\- probbit mcp
.fi
